into this zone.\n* **Zero Duplication Rate:** The dataset registers exactly **0 duplicate rows**, confirming that despite high internal sparsity, every record represents a unique transactional instance.\n\n---\n\n### Downstream Modeling Influence & Tactical Strategy\n\n1. **Strategic Feature Pruning (>90% Threshold):** Features exceeding 90% missingness (`col18`, `col19`, `col4`, `col5`) contain virtually zero statistical signal. Attempting to impute these columns would introduce massive synthetic noise and induce overfitting. These 4 features will be dropped entirely from the final training matrix.\n\n2. **Dual-Tier Numerical Imputation (`OperationalHoursMeter`):** Missing values in mechanical meters are rarely random; they often indicate unrecorded usage or older equipment. \n   * To capture this structural pattern, we will generate a binary indicator column: `Hours_isna = OperationalHoursMeter.isnull().astype(int)`.\n   * The original column will then be imputed using a robust central tendency metric (**Median**), which prevents the extreme right-hand outliers (e.g., the 1.7M hours anomaly) from biasing the imputed values.\n\n3. **Categorical Sentinel Encoding (`UtilizationTier`, `Spec_ReleaseSeries`, etc.):** Rather than forcing a mode imputation that artificially inflates the frequency of the majority class, all missing values in categorical columns will be mapped to a dedicated string sentinel like `'Missing'` or `'Unknown'`. Non-linear tree-based models (`LightGBM`, `CatBoost`) treat this as a distinct, valid structural state, allowing them to map specific risk or price profiles to unrecorded features natively.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(f\"unique items in train:\")\nprint(train.nunique())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-22T18:52:26.701594Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-22T18:52:26.701935Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-22T18:52:26.9151Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-22T18:52:26.70191Z"