onomic shifts. Because asset values drop during recessions regardless of physical quality, treating `TransactionDate` as a simple counter will fail. We must extract temporal components to create explicit macroeconomic indicators, such as **Yearly Market Liquidation Volume** and a **Recession Indicator Flag** (e.g., mapping the 2008–2011 downturn window) to adjust baseline value expectations.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Plot 3.11: Missingness heatmap correlation pattern\n\nmoderate_miss_cols=miss_df[miss_df['missing_%'].between(20, 80)].index.tolist()[:12]\nfig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 5))\nfig.suptitle('Plot 3.11: Missingness Correlation Pattern (Sample 2000 rows)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\nsns.heatmap(train[moderate_miss_cols].head(2000).isnull(),cbar=False,yticklabels=False,cmap='YlOrRd',ax=ax)\nax.set_xticklabels(ax.get_xticklabels(),rotation=45,ha='right',fontsize=9)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-22T18:53:23.438504Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-22T18:53:23.438855Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-22T18:53:23.670042Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-22T18:53:23.438817Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-22T18:53:23.669185Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1300x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":27},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n\n### Plot 3.11: Structural Missingness & Systemic Co-occurrence Maps\nA null-value matrix visualization isolating attributes with moderate missingness thresholds (20% to 80%) reveals that data missingness is not completely random (MNAR - Missing Not At Random):\n* **The Categorical Block-Null Pattern:** The matrix shows thick horizontal red blocks matching exactly across parallel feature subsets. For instance, when an entry is missing `col20`, it is simultaneously missing `col25` and `col21`. \n* **The Spec Collection Pipeline Break:** This pattern proves that missingness is dictated by structural collection failures during inventory entry. If an asset belongs to a specific configuration tier or is handled by a particular vendor partner, a whole block of descriptive characteristics is skipped by default.\n* **The Completeness Anchor (`UtilizationTier`):** In contrast, the sparse light-yellow bands in `UtilizationTier` indicate that this specific field operates independently of the other columns' missingness patterns.\n* **Engineering Impact:** This strong co-occurrence confirms that dropping features based on single column counts can destroy valuable group signals. It is highly recommended to create a unified missingness flag profile, such as a **Missingness Vector Hash** or an aggregated row-wise metric like `Total_Missing_Specs = df[spec_cols].isnull().sum(axis=1)`. This allows tree algorithms to use the missingness pattern itself as a powerful predictive feature.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 4. Feature Engineering & valdination","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4.1 Feature Engineering","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# =========================================================================\n# 4.1 FEATURE ENGINEERING\n# =========================================================================\nprint(\"Applying advanced feature engineering on raw data...\")\n\ndef engineer_features(df_in):\n    df = df_in.copy()\n    # Parse dates\n    df['TransactionDate'] = pd.to_datetime(df['TransactionDate'], errors='coerce')\n    df['Trans_Year'] = df['TransactionDate'].dt.year\n    df['Trans_Month'] = df['TransactionDate'].dt.month\n    df['Trans_DayOfWeek'] = df['TransactionDate'].dt.dayofweek\n\n    # Handle Year Anomaly (replace 1001 placeholder with NaN)\n    df['ManufactureYear_is_placeholder'] = (df['ManufactureYear'] == 1001).astype(int)\n    df.loc[df['ManufactureYear'] == 1001, 'ManufactureYear'] = np.nan\n    df['MachineAge'] = (df['Trans_Year'] - df['ManufactureYear']).clip(lower=0)\n\n    # Operational Hours Winsorization & log scaling\n    df['OperationalHoursMeter'] = df['OperationalHoursMeter'].clip(upper=60000)\n    df['LogHours'] = np.log1p(df['OperationalHoursMeter'])\n\n    # Usage Intensity\n    df['Usage_Intensity'] = df['OperationalHoursMeter'] / (df['MachineAge'] + 1)\n    df['LogUsage_Intensity'] = np.log1p(df['Usage_Intensity'])\n\n    return df\n\n# Transform raw datasets (assumes 'train' and 'test' are already loaded)\ntrain_eng = engineer_features(train)\ntest_eng  = engineer_features(test)\n\ny_log = np.log1p(train_eng['TargetValue'])\ndrop_cols = ['TransactionID', 'AssetID', 'TransactionDate', 'TargetValue', 'col18', 'col19', 'col4', 'col5','ManufactureYear','OperationalHoursMeter','Usage_Intensity']\nfeatures_raw = [col for col in train_eng.columns if col not in drop_cols]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-22T19:01:36.217115Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-22T19:01:36.217506Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-22T19:01:36.400253Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-22T19:01:36.217477Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-22T19:01:36.39917Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Applying advanced feature engineering on raw data...\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":49},{"cell_type":"code","source":"train_eng.info()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-22T19:01:39.705106Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-22T19:01:39.70547Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-22T19:01:39.949512Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-22T19:01:39.70544Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-22T19:01:39.94857Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\nRangeIndex: 138701 entries, 0 to 138700\nData columns (total 58 columns):\n #   Column                          Non-Null Count   Dtype         \n---  ------                          --------------   -----        